================================================================================
Third-party assets
================================================================================

roqsim's own code is Apache-2.0. The repository additionally VENDORS third-party robot descriptions,
meshes, textures, characters and scenes, each of which keeps its own license. Some of those licenses
(notably CC-BY-4.0) make ATTRIBUTION A CONDITION OF REDISTRIBUTION: if you redistribute this
repository, a package built from it, or the assets on their own, the corresponding notices must
travel with them.

The authoritative, per-asset records are:

  * a THIRD_PARTY.md in each package that vendors third-party content
        roqsim_assets/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_humanoid/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_quadruped/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_scenes/THIRD_PARTY.md
        roqsim_walker/THIRD_PARTY.md
  * a CREDITS.txt beside each individual asset (source URL, license, required attribution)
  * a license file beside each vendored robot model (e.g. models/ur10e/UR10e_LICENSE)

This file is a summary of those records, not a replacement for them.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Where the public/private line falls
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Vendored robot descriptions under BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0 / MPL-2.0 are redistributable and
re-fetchable from public upstreams, so they are shipped here. Curated artwork whose upstream is
gated behind an account or an API token is not shipped, even when its license would allow it.

